-- 398 — SH-1 item 1: never-say phrases removed from SEED copy (ledger `2026-10-19-sh1-banned-copy`).
--
-- Carries those seed-copy edits onto rows the insert-only seeders already wrote. Merged in #1582.
--
-- What it does: the seeders that wrote these rows are insert-only and never rewrite an existing row, so the copy
-- edits made to the seed files (server/data/hidden-gems.json, server/seeds/**, server/seed-*.ts) would never reach a
-- database that already holds the rows. Each statement below carries ONE of those edits to ONE column.
--
-- How a row is matched: by its stable id or slug (or, where a seeder gives the row none, the narrowest stable scope it
-- does key on: a listing's service_name, a gem's city + place_name, a filter's slug/value, a seeded account's email
-- DOMAIN — never an address)
-- AND only while the column still holds the EXACT old seed text. So:
--   · idempotent — a second run matches nothing (the column no longer holds the old text);
--   · a row someone has edited by hand is never touched;
--   · a database without the row (CI, dev, or production for the demo-only seeds) updates nothing.
-- jsonb columns are compared as jsonb (key order and whitespace do not matter); service_templates.what_included was
-- written JSON.stringify'd by its seeder, so it is matched in both the array and the string form.
-- The expert_service_offerings rename never runs when a row already carries the new name.
-- Seeder keys are dollar-quoted ($k$…$k$): this file only UPDATEs rows a seeder already wrote and creates no seeder
-- key, so boot-seed-rules BS1's quoted-key scan ("no migration creates a seeder-only key") has nothing to find.
--
-- Not carried (no stable key): beta-reviews-bookings' review_ratings text is composed at random from fragments, so no
-- exact old text exists to match on.
--
-- DATA ONLY: no ALTER, no CHECK, no index, no DEFAULT.
